@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.provisioning.license.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Provisioning License Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to provisioning and License Management works properly.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| Portal Production                               |
	| Commerce Subscription Development               |
	| Commerce Subscription Production                |
	| Commerce Subscription Non-Production            |
	| Commerce Subscription Backup                    |
	| Commerce Subscription Unlimited Enterprise-Wide |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                                  |
	| DXP Backup                                      |
	| DXP Non-Production                              |
	| Portal Production                               |
	| Platinum Subscription                           |
	| Gold Subscription                               |
	| Limited Subscription                            |
	| Enterprise Search for DXP Cloud - Prod          |
	| Commerce Subscription Production                |
	| Commerce Subscription Non-Production            |
	| Commerce Subscription Backup                    |
	| Commerce Subscription Unlimited Enterprise-Wide |
	| Commerce Subscription Development               |
	| Developer Services                              |
	| Analytics Cloud Basic                           |
	| Enterprise Search - Production                  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORLICKORLIC |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORLICKORLIC |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Generate new DXP license
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production (Production)   | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	When I click on the license with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Test Test                     | |
	When I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                | DXP Production |
	| Current Provisioned | 1              |
	| State               | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |

Scenario: Generate new DXP license via account subscription
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning via an account subscription

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button on the subscription details page
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Product | Select | DXP Production              | |
	| Version | Select | 7.2                         | |
	| Type    | Select | DXP Production (Production) | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	When I click on the license with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Test Test                     | |
	When I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                | DXP Production |
	| Current Provisioned | 1              |
	| State               | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product     | DXP Production                |
	| Type        | Production                    |
	| Host Name   | localhost                     |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Account Key: ${staticAccountKey} |
	| Label | Product: DXP Production          |

Scenario: Generate new complimentary DXP license
	Testing the ability to generate a new complimentary license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
